                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "height": 240
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "sGr24",
              "name": "Proposal notes — outside page designs",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$ss-surface",
              "cornerRadius": 14,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 16,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "KhSU7",
                  "name": "Proposes replacing",
                  "fill": "$ss-text",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Date-led list proposal: replace the image-first grid with compact chronological event rows and supporting thumbnails. Approved date treatment for this variant: a calendar tile with a lavender month strip and bold day, plus the year underneath. Desktop uses 80×112px tiles; mobile uses compact 56×88px tiles. Each complete event row remains one link; the date is informational, not a separate action.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "$ss-font",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "SUFT6",
                  "name": "Preserves",
                  "fill": "$ss-text",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Search & Discover First; visible title search and From / To fields; one shared range picker that applies only after both dates are selected; debounced title search; relevant filter resets; earliest event first; WIB times; visible Events, My Reservations and account access. Available, Fully Booked and Registration Closed remain discoverable. Registered replaces availability for an active reservation. Organizer-cancelled events are excluded.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "$ss-font",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "UTJ7B",
                  "name": "Small catalog behavior",
                  "fill": "$ss-text",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "The four rows are illustrative, not a hard limit. A single event retains the same date-led row. Empty results now use a quiet, left-aligned divider-led layout: no upcoming events has no recovery button; no matching results preserves entered filters and offers Clear all filters / Clear dates. Full desktop and mobile variants are provided. No pagination, infinite scrolling, fake scarcity or new booking features.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "$ss-font",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "JOT5W",
                  "name": "Accessibility and approval",
                  "fill": "$ss-text",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "All text remains selectable/editable. Rows have ample touch targets and should be implemented as one keyboard-focusable link with the existing lavender focus indicator. Date labels should be read as full dates, not disconnected numbers. Status text must remain in the accessible row name or description. Decorative separators need not reach 3:1; input boundaries and focus still require contrast testing. Midnight Social v0.2 tokens remain working defaults pending visual review.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.6,
                  "fontFamily": "$ss-font",
                  "fontSize": 14,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            },
